&#x000a9; 1970 by The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1970</copyright-year></permissions><abstract><p>Polyribocytidylate-<sup>3</sup>H-polyriboinosinate (rC-<sup>3</sup>H:rI) enters cultured rabbit kidney cells from the surrounding medium within &#x000bd; hr after exposure. Grains are found in the cytoplasm, nucleus, and nucleolus. At 2 hr, grains are localized predominantly over the nucleolar regions. Subsequently, the grains in the nucleus become dispersed. A specific receptor site for the initiation of interferon production was not revealed.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>